/* browser_hookup.spec.js Setup */

Configurations:

Chromium should be listed in your playwright.config.js.

projects: [
    {
      name: 'chromium',
      use: { ...devices['Desktop Chrome'] },
    }
]



Workflow: 

1. Open up a chromium based browser in debug mode. As long as localhost:9222 is reachable,
    this script can work.

e.g. For brave browser on Linux

    Syntax: <location of chromium browser executable> --<remote-debug-port> --<user-data-dir>

        brave --remote-debugging-port=9222 --user-data-dir="/tmp/playwright_brave_profile"

    Remote debugging port is to allow playwright to connect to your browser instance via CDP.
    User data dir stores all the cookies and login credentials for the session. You can specify
    a temporary folder to store the session data, or use an existing user data directory.

    Make sure the browser you open stays opened. Otherwise, you'll have to reopen it with the above
    command or find some way to start up your chromium-based browser of choice automatically in debug mode.

2. Login to any relevant websites to get past authentication. The session data will be stored in
    the user-data-dir you specify.

3. Run the browser_hookup.spec.js script:

    normal: npx playwright test browser_hookup.spec.js
    debug: npx playwright test browser_hookup.spec.js --debug